<p>President Donald Trump on Sunday rejected Iran’s response to the latest U.S. proposal to end the war, calling it “TOTALLY UNACCEPTABLE” after Tehran sent its reply through Pakistani mediators. Trump did not detail his objections. Iranian state media said Tehran’s response focused on ending the war on all fronts, including in Lebanon, and restoring security for shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. Iranian state television and semi-official Iranian media said Tehran’s terms included a halt to the U.S. naval blockade, recognition of Iranian sovereignty or control over the Strait of Hormuz, sanctions relief and compensation for war damage. Several sources described the war as about 10 weeks old, dating to February 28. It has disrupted Gulf shipping, pushed up energy prices and coincided with continued fighting involving Israel and Lebanon.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/EDSZnYGOSXW16YpwVAR2Lrtqmb0FLVuYao1jW538Gz9_qjiF7fpHicAAGX13IqLvRWwRRinsMg0tVR0TxGf662_2FnGhwDzKsIiG4YXvVmUF' alt='An Iranian man walks past an anti-US and anti-Israel mural painted on a wall, in the capital Tehran on May 10, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Iran warning: Iran said it would retaliate against any new U.S. strikes and would not permit more foreign warships in the Strait of Hormuz.</li><li>U.S. demands: U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright said Washington wanted traffic to flow freely through the Strait of Hormuz and sought an end to Iran’s nuclear program.</li><li>Diplomatic calendar: The rejection came four days before Trump’s planned summit with Chinese President Xi Jinping in Beijing, WSWS reported.</li></ul><blockquote>I have just read the response from Iran’s so-called ‘Representatives.’ I don’t like it TOTALLY UNACCEPTABLE - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He also told Axios that Iran’s letter was “inappropriate,” but declined to discuss its contents. (<a href='https://www.greaterkashmir.com/world/trump-rejects-irans-peace-proposal-as-totally-unacceptable-11821396'>Greater Kashmir</a>)</li><li>Iranian officials: Officials cited by Dawn said Tehran wanted to address hostilities first and leave sanctions relief and nuclear issues for later. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999294/trump-rejects-unacceptable-iranian-terms-for-ending-war'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright: Wright said Washington was still waiting for a “clear resolution” from Iran after weeks of stalled talks. (<a href='https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/national-international/iran-us-proposal-peace-talks/3933986/'>NBC Chicago</a>)</li><li>Republican Senator Lindsey Graham: Graham said Trump should consider military action if diplomatic efforts failed to change Tehran’s behavior. (<a href='https://www.greaterkashmir.com/world/trump-rejects-irans-peace-proposal-as-totally-unacceptable-11821396'>Greater Kashmir</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/05/11/kxdm-m11.html'>Trump calls Iranian response to negotiations “unacceptable,” as Israel continues Lebanon bloodbath</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3353071/trump-calls-irans-response-us-peace-proposal-unacceptable'>Trump calls Iran’s response to US peace proposal ‘unacceptable’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-rejects-iran-peace-terms-tehran-warns-of-new-attacks'>‘Totally unacceptable’: Trump rejects Iran peace terms as Tehran warns of new attacks</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/05/11/trump-calls-iran-s-response-to-his-peace-proposal-totally-unacceptable'>Trump calls Iran&#x27;s response to his peace proposal “totally unacceptable”</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/f66186e7-8e14-466d-b4de-114ee70c3e62'>Trump says Iran’s response to peace proposal is ‘unacceptable’</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05